# Comments: run top to bottom. Each login replaces the stored cookie.
# Nobody can edit or delete someone else's comment, not even the post's author.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:5174
@json = application/json

### 1. Log in as author1 and create a post to comment on
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

###
# @name post
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "A post to comment on", "content": "Say something." }

### 2. Comment on a draft -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "Too early" }

### 3. Publish it
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "published": true }

### 4. Log out, then comment anonymously -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "Who am I?" }

### 5. Log in as reader1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "reader1", "password": "{{$dotenv READER_PASSWORD}}" }

### 6. Comment -> 201 + Location. HTML is stored as written and escaped by the frontends.
# @name comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "<img src=x onerror=alert(1)> Great post!" }

### 7. Blank comment -> 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "   " }

### 8. Public list of the post's comments -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments

### 9. Edit my comment -> 200, editedAt set
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{comment.response.body.$.comment.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "Great post! (edited)" }

### 10. My comments, with the title of each post -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/comments

### 11. Log in as author1, the post's author
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 12. The post's author edits reader1's comment -> 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{comment.response.body.$.comment.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "content": "Censored" }

### 13. The post's author deletes reader1's comment -> 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{comment.response.body.$.comment.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

### 14. Clean up: delete the post (its comments go by Cascade) -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

### 15. The comment is gone with its post -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{post.response.body.$.post.id}}/comments
